      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-22T23:22:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "HID has tests involving \"reconnection\" i.e. we connect + bond, then disconnect, then reconnect. But the reconnection is currently failing since we are waiting for the BONDED intent which never arrives if we\u0027re already bonded.\n\nI could alternatively make two different methods: Reconnect() versus ConnectAndBond() - but that would require changing all the existing tests, most of which don\u0027t really care about the distinction (they just want to connect somehow).",
      "parentUuid": "b9066827_acf4d795",
      "revId": "458dca9bccd42998eb328e2b269b3334112c9f8d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d5e79b5f_02cbcfa2",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958203
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-22T23:24:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For example `TP/HCE/BV-04-I` (aka `HID/HOS/HCE/BV-04-I`) is \"Host initiated reconnection\"",
      "parentUuid": "498a5adb_41e6a641",
      "revId": "458dca9bccd42998eb328e2b269b3334112c9f8d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e90a166_131f9695",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1904823
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-22T23:53:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Approved as is, but I believe that waiting for `CONNECTED` may be problematic in some cases: the `CONNECTED` intent is sent after profiles are opened which may be an issue in some PTS test cases. Ideally, we should wait for `ACL_CONNECTED` but this intent is not correctly being sent right now 😞",
      "parentUuid": "d5e79b5f_02cbcfa2",
      "revId": "458dca9bccd42998eb328e2b269b3334112c9f8d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
